Backstage Forever normalization changes: separately compiled bounded quest
sharing counts, starting-item IDs, static durations, reported item/count drops,
four-source exact-ID/name trainer joins and observed service listings, and
status-valid enUS item names. Malformed optional rows are omitted and counted.
Each build is normalized separately and the results are merged newest-first:
rows are unioned by exact ID, scalar facts come from the newest build, trainer
positions, observed reactions and service listings are unioned with caps, and a
reported service level replaces an unknown (zero) one. When a build's creature
cache lacks a trainer, its enUS title may come from another pinned build's
record with the same exact ID and name.
Descriptions, costs, ambiguous abilities, narrative text, race masks, game
assets and personal saved records are excluded. Per-file metadata, byte sizes,
hashes and immutable URLs are preserved in pack.json/source-lock.json.

Compilation and player observations are licensed by Efficient Games. The
files are from one publisher, not independent witnesses. Observation
names have unspecified locale; enUS cache names do not establish their locale.
Counts describe source saved files/recorded answers (the largest single-build
count after merging), not distinct people, independent witnesses, confidence
or probabilities. Level zero remains unknown
requirement/already-known ambiguity. Positive levels are reported levels, not
learned status or proof of eligibility. Positions approximate where a window
was opened; current location, faction access and availability remain unknown.

This license does not grant rights in Blizzard narrative text or game assets.
This supplementary artifact updates with the application only. The existing
quest-reference refresh remains a separate six-file feature.
